{
  "milestone": "Local application-error unions and transparent aliases",
  "date": "2026-10-19",
  "baseline_commit": "5269a128522b7b98a1070b95ef1b565961cc6b7f",
  "host": "Apple M2 Max / macOS arm64",
  "implementation": {
    "typing": "Canonical sets of original declared application-error families; nested/duplicated/reordered aliases normalize identically. Subset propagation and direct fallible returns widen explicitly, with exhaustive original-family-qualified handlers.",
    "representation": "Private flattened tagged aggregates preserve original family/variant identity and exact field types. Widening remaps the selected variant and retains active backing without interpreting an absent success payload.",
    "ownership": "Both active union families verified through cached observations, scheduler teardown, malformed descriptors, partial-retention failure and inactive-arm isolation.",
    "control_flow": "Synthesized enum-match dispatch adopts intermediate error obligations, permitting mixed success/fail arms without a spurious discarded-error diagnostic.",
    "limits": [
      "TaskError composition and application-error task/parallel boundaries remain gated.",
      "Record/enum payload fields continue to use original family types rather than error aliases.",
      "fail error retains the entire union; selected-family reconstruction narrows it. Whole-value match-arm flow narrowing remains follow-up work.",
      "No general value unions, public C/C++ ABI, distributed schemas or GPU error transport."
    ]
  },
